> Here are my questions:
> -What's my best bet of finding an attack spellbook?  I'm pretty sure
> I've cleared all the shops, but I'll double check.

Guillotine the castle occupants, make sure luck is maxed, and wish for
a magic marker (usually at least a couple of the castle wand wishes go
for markers).  Use it to write magic missile in a blanked spellbook
(wizards with maxed luck have a very high probability of doing this).

> -Should I throw some of my 17 stack of daggers to help clear the
> castle, even though if I get stuck and have to retreat, they'll then
> be in a monster infested area and likely hard to retrieve?

Guillotine them with the drawbridge.  Even an XL1 character with a
(semi-) permanent Elbereth and an instrument can usually clear the
castle (beware sharks one-hitting you, and you may need to get
creative if there's a minotaur around--?earth from Sokoban can help),
though they'll be much over XL1 when they're done.

> -If I do manage to get to the wand of wishing in the castle, what
> should I wish for?  I think 2 blessed scrolls of charging is the first
> priority, then a magic marker, and then a BoH.  Any other suggestions?

More markers if you need them, otherwise save the wishes.  You have MR
and reflection, those merit wishes too.  I'd investigate the odds of
just getting a blessed marker first and writing charging with it (max
your luck), if it's at least 0:2 to start with that's almost certainly
the right move.



